'''''Pellaea viridis''''', known as the '''green cliff brake''', is a type of fern indigenous to regions including Africa, Yemen, some Pacific Ocean islands and India. However it is an invasive species in Australia.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Pellaea viridis'', PlantNET - NSW Flora Online, retrieved July 12th, 2017|url=http://plantnet.rbgsyd.nsw.gov.au/cgi-bin/NSWfl.pl?page=nswfl&lvl=sp&name=Pellaea~viridis}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=''Pellaea viridis'', U.S. National Plant Germplasm System, retrieved July 12th, 2017|url=https://npgsweb.ars-grin.gov/gringlobal/taxonomydetail.aspx?id=407072}}</ref>

